WEBVTT

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:04.900
One, two...

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:07.680
Do we have any this month?

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:08.960
Um...

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:10.280
Oh, there.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:11.070
When?

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:12.800
There. Saturday.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:14.610
You're right. Nice!

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:18.700
Who would have thought it'd be so rare 
for your days off to line up?

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:21.370
We never get the same days off.

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:23.370
We have a lot of staff, too.

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:25.990
And with early and late shifts, 
it's really hard.

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:30.090
Wait. We're closing on that day.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:33.070
Wow, you, too, Udon-chan?

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:35.070
Let's all hang out together again!

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:36.010
Sounds good!

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:39.010
Oh, yeah, there's something 
I've been wanting to do.

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.490
<b>Hangout Spot
Kuragefuu</b>

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:21.700
"Hangout Spot Umitsuki... kaze"?

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:26.500
Yonekura Marina-san?

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:29.750
Oh, you're from marketing!

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:31.640
Maeda Akari.

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:34.520
Did you get the invitation email, too?

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:35.340
Yeah.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:37.150
Is this the right room?

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:38.720
I believe so.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:40.510
Welcome!

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:42.120
You're the first ones here.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:43.130
Welcome.

00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:44.310
Come on in!

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:46.810
Thanks for having us.

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:50.720
I'm surprised.

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:52.780
It's actually clean here.

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:54.490
What is that supposed to mean?

00:02:54.490 --> 00:02:57.280
Your desk at work is really messy.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:00.920
That's because the assistant director 
keeps giving me so much work!

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:00.920
It's okay.

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:02.700
Let's start with introductions.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:05.420
Was that an impression of Chief Garandou?

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:07.200
No, it wasn't!

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:09.960
Kukuru, please.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:11.310
Oh, sorry.

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:13.140
You know Akari-chan, right?

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:15.630
I've been to the shop a few times.

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:18.700
This is the penguin attendant, Marina-san.

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:20.880
Hi, nice to meet you.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:25.070
This is Hangout Spot Kuragefuu's 
Chef Teruya Tsukimi.

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:26.480
Also known as Udon-chan.

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:28.650
I love udon.

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:31.260
I'm training at a café called Ohana.

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:32.520
You should come eat sometime.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.060
Although we don't serve udon.

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:35.640
I'll be there.

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:36.720
Thanks.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:38.360
I'll make some drinks.

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:41.240
Oh, don't mind me. 
I brought something.

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:43.160
I bought some mangoes.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:44.280
Let's eat.

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:45.950
No! Jeez!

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:49.080
We called it a get-together, 
but it's supposed to be a hospitality party.

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:50.870
"A hospitality party"?

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:53.680
Everyone's always working their butts off,

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:56.760
so we wanted to give them a chance 
to relax and do nothing.

00:03:56.760 --> 00:04:01.670
We'll serve you, 
so just relax to your heart's content.

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:03.900
I'd feel bad.

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:06.460
In that case, I'll relax!

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:12.940
Come on, Akari-chan. Relax.

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:15.470
Loosen up.

00:04:15.470 --> 00:04:17.190
But...

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.780
Here you are.

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:20.150
Your tropical tea.

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:22.320
I used your mangoes, too, Marina-san.

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:24.380
Looks good!

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:25.410
It's so cute!

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:27.340
What would you like for breakfast?

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:28.360
Meat.

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:29.440
In the morning?

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:31.160
Yeah. I love meat.

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:33.560
Do you have sandwiches or anything?

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:35.120
Coming right up!

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:40.220
That's from our aquarium.

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:41.520
Although it's closed now.

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:44.560
I know. I've been to Gama Gama before.

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:45.870
Really?

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:48.720
It was so laid-back and comfortable.

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:51.130
It was really different from Tingarla.

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:52.980
True.

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:55.980
They're both nice aquariums.

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:00.480
Why did you decide to become
an attendant, Marina-san?

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:02.970
Because it was easy.

00:05:02.970 --> 00:05:04.780
It's tough being an attendant.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:07.230
I don't mean that.

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:09.470
Japanese is hard.

00:05:09.470 --> 00:05:13.340
It was really hard in the beginning.
I kept miscommunicating.

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:17.370
But you don't need words 
to communicate with sea life.

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:18.920
It was super easy.

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:20.490
I know what you mean!

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:23.010
What's the first animal 
you had an understanding with?

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:24.240
Squid.

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:25.930
Bigfin reef squid? Purpleback flying squid?

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:26.970
Cuttlefish!

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:28.480
It sprayed ink on me!

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:30.780
I got sprayed on, too!

00:05:31.190 --> 00:05:32.060
Buddies!

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:35.930
Are attendants always having 
conversations like that?

00:05:35.930 --> 00:05:37.150
They are.

00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:39.440
I got creeped out at first, too.

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:41.020
Fuuka-san...

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:44.530
You're so smooth!

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:47.640
Kukuru-san's cheeks are nice 
and plump, too.

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:50.190
But your cheeks are beautiful, too!

00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:51.910
Th-Thanks.

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:57.720
I've been looking forward to the skincare lesson 
you wrote about in the invitation email.

00:05:57.720 --> 00:05:59.920
Are you going to teach us?

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:01.050
Yes.

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:05.300
My stylist from way back 
gave me some advice.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:07.930
A professional stylist! Wow!

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:09.050
What's going on?

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:12.010
Would you like to get in 
on the skincare lesson?

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:13.580
Yes! I'm in!

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:14.720
Yay!

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:18.190
Well, let's go to the second house.

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:20.940
<b>Hospitality Spot Kuragefuu 
Second Home</b>

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:20.940
In order to have good skin,

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:23.100
not only do you need 
to avoid sunburn,

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:25.690
but you also have to work on 
keeping your skin hydrated as well.

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:28.850
Choose the right toner
for your skin, apply generously,

00:06:28.850 --> 00:06:30.140
and let it sink in.

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:33.370
The trick is to trap
the moisture in your skin.

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:36.580
Become pretty.

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:38.960
Become pretty.

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:46.590
Become pretty.

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:46.590
Hi!

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:48.220
Sorry we're late!

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:49.340
'Sup.

00:06:49.890 --> 00:06:52.590
Become pretty.

00:06:52.590 --> 00:06:54.160
Become pretty.

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:56.100
Nope! Nope! Nope!

00:06:57.220 --> 00:06:59.800
Kuuya-san, it's nice and cold.

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:05.390
It's so smooth!

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:07.780
My skin's so happy.

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:10.680
Hey, what about Kuuya-san?

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:12.190
It's fine.

00:07:12.190 --> 00:07:14.140
He's afraid of girls.

00:07:14.140 --> 00:07:15.030
Huh.

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:17.820
He's gotten a lot better, though.

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:20.000
A while back, 
he would have just gone home.

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:31.460
Here you are.

00:07:32.990 --> 00:07:35.470
I hope you enjoy.

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:37.010
Thank you!

00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:41.890
It's delicious.

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:43.340
Awesome!

00:07:43.340 --> 00:07:44.940
I could eat these forever.

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:46.500
It's so juicy!

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:49.030
Could you give me some criticism, too?

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:51.030
What do you mean?

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:56.920
If you just tell me it's delicious, 
I'm not going to be able to grow.

00:07:56.920 --> 00:08:00.780
I think it's important 
to listen to negative feedback.

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:03.120
Don't you ask the people at work?

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:05.670
It gets too technical.

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:09.040
I want some honest feedback 
from customers.

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:10.170
Please!

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:14.840
I might prefer bite-sized sandwiches.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:16.890
So that I don't get my lipstick on it.

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:18.360
I see.

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:21.180
I think the sauce could be a bit stronger.

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:24.310
And the meat's a bit tough.

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:26.360
The sandwich ingredients are kinda plain.

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:27.640
I'd like some oranges.

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:29.390
I might get bored part way.

00:08:29.390 --> 00:08:30.970
The meat's kinda bleh 
once it gets cold!

00:08:30.970 --> 00:08:32.900
You're right. It's getting dry!

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:34.330
Stop!

00:08:34.330 --> 00:08:35.260
That's plenty!

00:08:35.260 --> 00:08:37.660
Aw, you asked.

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:40.410
Sorry, that's as much damage 
as I can take.

00:08:45.220 --> 00:08:46.220
Where are you going?

00:08:46.220 --> 00:08:47.400
Bathroom.

00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:49.130
The bathroom's there.

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:51.160
That's the girl's bathroom.

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:53.130
I'll go find a park.

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:54.860
See you.

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:02.140
This one!

00:09:03.280 --> 00:09:05.220
Yay!

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:08.000
I lost again.

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:09.190
You suck at this.

00:09:09.970 --> 00:09:12.070
Marina-san, are you good for time?

00:09:13.910 --> 00:09:14.990
Shoot.

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:17.280
That was relaxing.

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:19.690
I'm recharged for work.

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:21.490
I'm glad.

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:24.800
I'll tell Chiyu-san to drop by, 
since she has the early shift.

00:09:24.800 --> 00:09:27.500
I'm sure she's starved for relaxation.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:28.250
See you!

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:29.710
Bye.

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:31.250
Take care!

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:34.260
All right, I'm winning the next one!

00:09:55.680 --> 00:09:57.770
You could stay longer.

00:09:57.770 --> 00:10:00.350
Yeah. Make yourselves at home.

00:10:00.350 --> 00:10:02.720
The early shift people are coming, right?

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:05.370
It'll get too crowded.

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:08.240
I have some plans after.

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:10.270
Thank you for everything today.

00:10:10.270 --> 00:10:13.050
The skincare lesson was really useful.

00:10:13.570 --> 00:10:14.780
See you soon.

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:16.330
Bye-bye.

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:21.550
What happened to Kuuya-san?

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:23.500
I totally forgot about him!

00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:27.030
Maybe he went home satisfied 
after he had Grams's plum wine.

00:10:29.830 --> 00:10:30.890
Good evening.

00:10:30.890 --> 00:10:32.240
Hello.

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:33.860
Thanks for inviting us.

00:10:35.410 --> 00:10:37.360
I'm glad you came.

00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:41.390
You said there'd be dinner, 
and that you'd babysit my son, so...

00:10:41.390 --> 00:10:44.790
Besides, Marina-san gave 
a strong recommendation.

00:10:45.130 --> 00:10:47.660
You should totally go, Chiyu-san!

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:50.670
You'll never have a chance 
like this again.

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:53.040
That much?

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:56.460
We've set up a special menu 
for the night shift.

00:10:56.830 --> 00:10:58.380
A special menu?

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:02.340
Chiyu-san, you first. 
Would you come to the next room?

00:11:03.590 --> 00:11:04.500
Okay.

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:08.300
Shizu-kun, I'm going 
to borrow Mommy for a bit.

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:10.060
Have fun with the nice lady.

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:13.150
Okay, I will. See you!

00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:18.810
Are those two okay by themselves?

00:11:18.810 --> 00:11:21.710
Kukuru just wants Chiyu-san to relax.

00:11:21.710 --> 00:11:22.540
Don't worry.

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:24.000
Wait, no!

00:11:24.490 --> 00:11:26.860
I said "no"! Stop!

00:11:25.640 --> 00:11:27.990
<b>Hangout Spot Kuragefuu</b>

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:30.460
What are you doing?

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:33.210
Don't be such a sore loser.

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:35.000
Hurry up and get undressed.

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:37.420
You don't need to be shy.

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:41.220
No, no, why should I get
undressed in front of you?

00:11:41.780 --> 00:11:43.970
If you don't, we can't do it.

00:11:44.770 --> 00:11:46.390
Aroma massage.

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:49.210
Huh?

00:11:55.260 --> 00:11:57.520
You have such nice skin.

00:11:57.900 --> 00:12:01.280
I don't know how many years it's been.

00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:03.240
It was Fuuka's idea.

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:06.520
That the scent would be comforting, 
and it would help with exhaustion.

00:12:06.520 --> 00:12:09.240
It really does smell nice.

00:12:09.240 --> 00:12:11.160
It's chamemoli.

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:12.780
You mean "chamomile."

00:12:14.680 --> 00:12:15.790
Yeah, that.

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:19.550
Apparently it has a calming effect 
and helps you sleep.

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:20.990
I know.

00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:22.250
I'm sure you're tired.

00:12:22.250 --> 00:12:24.260
You can take a nap if you'd like.

00:12:25.520 --> 00:12:31.060
I'd love to do that, 
but there's a bit of a problem.

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:32.460
What's that?

00:12:32.460 --> 00:12:33.700
You suck.

00:12:34.640 --> 00:12:36.160
But I'm rubbing...

00:12:36.160 --> 00:12:37.400
Am I off?

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:38.970
No, no.

00:12:38.160 --> 00:12:39.100
Where?

00:12:38.970 --> 00:12:40.960
Ow, ow, ow!

00:12:39.100 --> 00:12:41.180
Here?

00:12:40.960 --> 00:12:42.900
Wait! No!

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:42.900
Here? It's here!

00:12:44.840 --> 00:12:46.700
This is so nice.

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:49.240
I'm sorry.

00:12:49.240 --> 00:12:52.040
I knew it. 
You don't have any knots at all.

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:55.870
Most people who don't get knots 
suck at giving massages.

00:12:56.190 --> 00:13:00.540
I used to rub my Gramps and Grams's
shoulders a lot when I was a kid, though.

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:03.090
They were both happy.

00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:05.100
They were being nice.

00:13:05.100 --> 00:13:06.840
They adore their grandkid.

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:08.840
Is that really it?

00:13:09.910 --> 00:13:11.600
That's why he had the massager!

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:18.540
Even though I was massaging his back 
all the time, one day, he'd bought a massager.

00:13:19.010 --> 00:13:22.090
Could he not take my shoulder rubs anymore?

00:13:24.440 --> 00:13:27.870
Only Grams and Gramps know the truth, huh?

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:28.910
There, done.

00:13:29.310 --> 00:13:31.620
Sorry, I'll do it again!

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:32.760
It's fine.

00:13:32.760 --> 00:13:34.560
I'm better off doing it myself.

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:36.190
Please don't say that!

00:13:36.190 --> 00:13:37.740
Hospitality is...

00:13:39.410 --> 00:13:40.670
Is everything all right?

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:42.480
Nice timing.

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:44.380
You should do Kaoru next.

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:46.260
I need to check on Shizuku anyway.

00:13:47.490 --> 00:13:49.220
It's lots of fun.

00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:50.760
What's going on?

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:52.640
Get undressed.

00:13:53.570 --> 00:13:55.270
Aroma massage.

00:13:56.240 --> 00:13:57.690
I'll pass.

00:13:57.690 --> 00:13:59.520
I don't like wriggling sensations.

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:00.800
It's all right.

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:02.400
I'll give it everything I've got.

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:04.900
That's not the point.

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:07.650
Please!

00:14:11.690 --> 00:14:13.020
Is that a seal?

00:14:13.020 --> 00:14:14.010
Huh?

00:14:14.010 --> 00:14:15.370
It can't be.

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:19.780
Isn't that...

00:14:26.240 --> 00:14:31.650
Based on my observations, 
this is the common work senpai.

00:14:31.650 --> 00:14:32.850
Seriously?

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:35.850
Nope. Nope. Nope.

00:14:36.710 --> 00:14:38.360
Look at all the stars.

00:14:38.360 --> 00:14:41.610
It's so quiet that it's almost lonely.

00:14:42.500 --> 00:14:44.110
'Sup!

00:14:44.110 --> 00:14:45.210
Huh?

00:14:45.210 --> 00:14:47.070
Kuuya-san, I thought you went home.

00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:48.760
We captured him over there.

00:14:48.760 --> 00:14:51.490
He seems to have ran out of strength 
on his way back here.

00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:53.680
I can finally drink with the boys.

00:14:53.680 --> 00:14:55.290
Let's get started!

00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:57.710
He's like a different person.

00:14:57.710 --> 00:14:59.750
He's revived now, with the guys here.

00:15:00.280 --> 00:15:01.820
Let's drink.

00:15:01.820 --> 00:15:03.210
Pardon us.

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:04.460
Where is she?

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:07.340
Beauty treatments in Fuuka's room with Kaoru-san.

00:15:07.340 --> 00:15:09.760
She might be butt naked 
right about now.

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:10.760
What?

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:12.810
I'm borrowing the kitchen.

00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:14.110
Oh, I'll...

00:15:14.110 --> 00:15:15.470
It's fine.

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:20.330
Not bad.

00:15:20.330 --> 00:15:22.230
I guess you're a fisherman's kid, after all.

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:25.210
What's this?

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:26.650
It's a takoyaki grill.

00:15:27.220 --> 00:15:31.030
There was someone from Kansai 
in my seminar class, so I've mastered grilling.

00:15:31.030 --> 00:15:33.580
This is my first time at a takoyaki party.

00:15:33.580 --> 00:15:35.720
This isn't just an ordinary takoyaki party.

00:15:35.720 --> 00:15:38.670
We'll take the opportunity 
to turn it into a game.

00:15:38.670 --> 00:15:39.580
I call it...

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:42.320
"It's a takoyaki, but it's not octopus?!

00:15:42.320 --> 00:15:45.210
Get it right, and you're
the king of the aquarium!"

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:46.290
Puff puff!

00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:50.260
Here we go!

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:51.710
The rules are simple.

00:15:51.710 --> 00:15:54.220
Eat a takoyaki and guess what's inside.

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:59.060
It'll be a test of your understanding 
and love of sea life.

00:15:59.320 --> 00:16:00.360
Love?

00:16:00.360 --> 00:16:01.840
I'm not sure I'll get it.

00:16:01.840 --> 00:16:03.140
All right, for round one...

00:16:03.140 --> 00:16:04.510
I'm up!

00:16:04.510 --> 00:16:06.570
Shizu-kun, let's team up.

00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:07.270
Okay.

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:10.090
We're up against Eiji-kun.

00:16:10.090 --> 00:16:13.770
I've always wanted to do a marine-life 
quiz-off against Eiji-kun.

00:16:13.770 --> 00:16:15.620
No, I'm the host.

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:18.010
Why not? He's challenging you.

00:16:18.010 --> 00:16:20.570
Okay, put on your blindfolds.

00:16:20.570 --> 00:16:22.260
Are you serious?

00:16:23.580 --> 00:16:25.700
I can do it myself.

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:48.410
Wow.

00:16:48.410 --> 00:16:49.780
Not bad.

00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:51.780
Okay, first question.

00:16:51.780 --> 00:16:53.110
What's this?

00:16:53.110 --> 00:16:54.060
Here.

00:17:02.260 --> 00:17:03.750
What's this?

00:17:04.360 --> 00:17:05.370
Can you guess?

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:08.000
Fish?

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:09.850
Good job.

00:17:09.850 --> 00:17:11.100
Which fish?

00:17:11.100 --> 00:17:12.650
Oh! It's mackerel!

00:17:12.650 --> 00:17:14.800
Nope, it's not just any mackerel.

00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:16.760
Cured mackerel.

00:17:16.760 --> 00:17:18.910
Cured mackerel! Correct!

00:17:18.910 --> 00:17:20.100
Wow.

00:17:20.380 --> 00:17:22.020
Moving on, question number two.

00:17:28.100 --> 00:17:29.360
Flying fish roe?

00:17:29.360 --> 00:17:30.330
No.

00:17:30.330 --> 00:17:32.180
Based on my analysis...

00:17:32.610 --> 00:17:33.740
These are sea grapes!

00:17:34.040 --> 00:17:34.920
Bingo!

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:35.700
Sea grapes.

00:17:36.770 --> 00:17:37.700
I'll get the next one!

00:17:38.010 --> 00:17:39.260
You aren't beating me.

00:17:39.260 --> 00:17:41.200
The salmon's yummy.

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:42.560
No fair.

00:17:42.560 --> 00:17:44.300
Leave some for Mommy.

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:45.980
Say "ah."

00:17:45.980 --> 00:17:47.500
What happened to the game?

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:49.630
It was a serious battle.

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:52.270
You'll enjoy it more 
if you just eat it normally.

00:17:52.270 --> 00:17:53.120
Yum.

00:17:53.120 --> 00:17:54.090
More, please!

00:17:54.090 --> 00:17:54.630
Right?

00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:00.260
We're back!

00:18:00.950 --> 00:18:02.920
Huh, Kai, you're here.

00:18:02.920 --> 00:18:04.270
It's packed.

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:05.800
Scooch over.

00:18:05.800 --> 00:18:07.340
You're sitting here?

00:18:07.340 --> 00:18:08.600
Got a problem?

00:18:08.890 --> 00:18:10.540
Come on. Make some more!

00:18:10.540 --> 00:18:12.360
You're such a slave driver.

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:14.780
I'm starving!

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:23.710
I'm stuffed.

00:18:23.710 --> 00:18:25.410
Aquarium King...

00:18:25.760 --> 00:18:28.140
Should we get going, Shizu-kun?

00:18:28.720 --> 00:18:30.010
I want to stay longer.

00:18:30.010 --> 00:18:32.040
It's bedtime soon.

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:33.340
No bedtime.

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:35.760
How about some fireworks to end with?

00:18:36.250 --> 00:18:39.230
Let's go home after fireworks, okay?

00:18:39.230 --> 00:18:40.260
Okay!

00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:52.890
It's so pretty.

00:18:52.890 --> 00:18:54.820
Good for us, huh, Shizu-kun?

00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:01.610
Here.

00:19:01.930 --> 00:19:03.620
S-So dull...

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:08.330
Kukuru, what's up?

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:10.080
I'm glad we did this.

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:12.160
I think everyone enjoyed it.

00:19:12.160 --> 00:19:13.150
Yeah.

00:19:13.150 --> 00:19:16.380
It's thanks to your idea, Fuuka-chan.

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:17.340
Nah.

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:22.410
I just wanted Chiyu-san to get a bit 
of a break from working so hard.

00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:29.130
And I got some valuable feedback, too.

00:19:29.130 --> 00:19:31.850
I'm going to crank out 
some new menu items starting tomorrow!

00:19:32.160 --> 00:19:33.310
We'll be there to try it.

00:19:33.310 --> 00:19:34.560
You'd better.

00:19:34.560 --> 00:19:37.600
You two should come more often.

00:19:37.600 --> 00:19:39.530
We'll go once we get paid.

00:19:40.770 --> 00:19:43.020
Kuuya-san, how are you getting home?

00:19:43.020 --> 00:19:45.370
You aren't sober yet, are you?

00:19:45.370 --> 00:19:46.780
Do you live far?

00:19:46.780 --> 00:19:48.170
I live in Nanjo.

00:19:48.170 --> 00:19:48.860
That's far.

00:19:48.860 --> 00:19:50.540
You should move.

00:19:50.540 --> 00:19:53.320
I can bike to work.

00:19:53.320 --> 00:19:56.540
My Grams' got bad legs, 
so I can't leave her behind.

00:19:56.540 --> 00:19:58.910
You're kind, huh?

00:19:58.910 --> 00:20:00.330
That's normal.

00:20:00.330 --> 00:20:02.700
No, I didn't expect that from you.

00:20:02.700 --> 00:20:04.140
What do you mean by that?

00:20:04.490 --> 00:20:06.970
When should we do takoyaki again?

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:09.140
We need to settle the score.

00:20:10.720 --> 00:20:12.060
Fireworks!

00:20:12.060 --> 00:20:13.520
Youth, eh?

00:20:13.520 --> 00:20:15.560
Umi-yan, you're late.

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:16.910
We were waiting for you.

00:20:16.910 --> 00:20:20.760
I figured the young'uns would prefer 
to be by themselves.

00:20:20.760 --> 00:20:22.680
Here's a gift.

00:20:22.680 --> 00:20:24.640
Thanks!

00:20:24.640 --> 00:20:27.490
The missus sent me some 
from the islands.

00:20:28.340 --> 00:20:30.080
You're married, Umi-yan?

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:31.700
Yeah.

00:20:32.030 --> 00:20:33.680
A mystery of the universe...

00:20:33.680 --> 00:20:36.270
Huh? Chief Garandou.

00:20:36.270 --> 00:20:38.440
He had a lot to get off his chest.

00:20:38.440 --> 00:20:40.310
I was hearing him out.

00:20:40.740 --> 00:20:41.800
Oh, yeah.

00:20:42.400 --> 00:20:44.340
Kuuya, want a ride?

00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:45.320
Godly!

00:20:45.320 --> 00:20:46.260
Thanks!

00:20:47.110 --> 00:20:49.210
Want to call it a day?

00:20:49.210 --> 00:20:50.090
Okay.

00:20:58.400 --> 00:20:59.560
See you.

00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:00.040
Bye.

00:20:59.560 --> 00:21:00.650
Later.

00:21:00.990 --> 00:21:02.550
Bye-bye.

00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:10.080
<b>Morning, how are things? 

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:12.580
A reward?!

00:21:15.280 --> 00:21:16.830
When did she do that?

00:21:17.280 --> 00:21:19.130
Let's eat!

00:21:22.260 --> 00:21:23.420
It's so good!

00:21:23.420 --> 00:21:24.590
Bliss!

00:21:33.480 --> 00:21:35.550
Sorry, I just remembered something.

00:21:35.550 --> 00:21:36.310
What?

00:21:36.640 --> 00:21:39.810
I didn't think Kaoru-san would
hate massages so much.

00:21:39.810 --> 00:21:43.610
Yeah, I didn't think she'd be so against it.

00:21:43.610 --> 00:21:46.440
Haebaru-san told me I sucked, too.

00:21:46.840 --> 00:21:49.740
Marina-san's squid story 
was surprising, though!

00:21:49.740 --> 00:21:51.640
So was Eiji-san's battle cry.

00:21:51.640 --> 00:21:54.330
I didn't expect him to do "puff puff."

00:21:54.330 --> 00:21:55.750
Huh? Say what?

00:21:55.750 --> 00:21:57.990
So, when we were doing takoyaki,

00:21:58.390 --> 00:22:02.600
Eiji put on this proper face and started talking 
about an aquarium king quiz

00:22:02.600 --> 00:22:04.380
and saying "puff puff" and stuff.

00:22:04.380 --> 00:22:05.900
Say what?
